A1. This can be found at the end of an Egyptian cigarette. ~ ASH
A4. A very beastly King, indeed. ~ LEO
A7. Nickname for the cough that carries them off. ~ FLU
A10. The cry of a chicken. ~ PEEP
A12. This has four legs and plays in the parlor. ~ PIANO
A14. There's a lot of these in this puzzle. ~ TEES
A15. Veterans who often fly to arms. ~ TARS
A16. This eats fish in an expensive coat. ~ OTTER
A17. What angry aviators fly into. ~ RAGE
A18. It's difficult to get over these—on Sundays especially. ~ ROADS
A20. By what you can tell Horizontal 15 a long way off? ~ GAITS
